---
description: Core standards for the Eman Bakery platform — always apply
alwaysApply: true
---

- The single source of truth for features and behavior is `docs/SPEC.md`. The execution order is `BUILD_PLAN.md`. Operating rules are `AGENTS.md`. Read all three before writing code in a new session.
- Never hard-delete a financial record (orders, order_items, payments, ledger_transactions, customer_product_prices, audit_logs). Deactivate or reverse instead.
- Every table holding customer or financial data must have Row Level Security enabled with policies matching the role matrix in `docs/SPEC.md` §5.2 — no exceptions, no "temporary" open policies.
- Compute prices, totals, and balances server-side, always — never trust a value the client sent for anything financial.
- Match the Dark Luxury design system and motion spec in `docs/SPEC.md` §2 for any new UI — don't introduce a different visual or animation language.
- Use the shared components already defined in `docs/SPEC.md` §2.3 (DataTable, MoneyDisplay, ConfirmDialog) rather than re-implementing per page.
- TypeScript strict mode, ESLint, and Prettier must be clean before a commit.
